Brain Exposome — licence
========================

Data
----

The datasets this project compiles and publishes — the files under `public/data/` and
the values shown on https://brain-exposome.mattye.dev — are licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0).

    Deed        https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Legal code  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Attribute as:

    Brain Exposome — https://brain-exposome.mattye.dev

The full licence text is not reproduced here; the deed and legal code above are the
authoritative wording.


Exception — modelled dementia prevalence
----------------------------------------

`public/data/dementia/` derives from GBD 2023 age-specific rates published by the
Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME). IHME releases GBD under a
free-of-charge **non-commercial, attribution** agreement:

    https://www.healthdata.org/Data-tools-practices/data-practices/ihme-free-charge-non-commercial-user-agreement

CC BY 4.0 permits commercial reuse. This project therefore cannot pass that right on for
GBD-derived values. **The dementia layer is available for non-commercial use with
attribution only**, and reuse must credit both this project and:

    Global Burden of Disease Study 2023 (GBD 2023),
    Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)

This is why the schema.org Dataset node for that layer states a different licence from
the others — see `src/lib/dataset-ld.mjs`.


Upstream sources keep their own terms
-------------------------------------

The CC BY 4.0 grant above covers this project's compilation, derivation and
presentation. It does not — and cannot — relicense the sources those values come from.
Every record carries its own `source` field, and each schema.org Dataset node lists its
sources in `isBasedOn`. Terms that matter in practice:

    ACAG SatPM2.5 V6.GL.03 (WashU)     CC BY 4.0
    WorldPop 2020 1km age/sex grids    CC BY 4.0
    Natural Earth boundaries           public domain
    National statistics offices        each its own terms; see the per-record source
    GBD 2023 (IHME)                    non-commercial + attribution — see the exception
    Korea MOHW / NID dementia status   KOGL Type 1 (attribution) — KR dementia layer
    Livingston et al., Lancet 2024     relative risks quoted with citation

Raw upstream files are deliberately not redistributed here; only derived per-unit values
are published (see docs/dementia-exposome/data-refresh-workflow.md).


